From: whitebelyash <whbexiumwork@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] u_gralloc: always use the UBWC detection path

u_gralloc checks whether a buffer was allocated by the Qualcomm vendor
gralloc by comparing the 'gmsm' magic with the buffer handle data. Newer
gralloc versions no longer store it, so the check never succeeded and the
buffer never got the proper DRM format modifier, which caused a heavily
distorted picture on screen.

Based on whitebelyash/mesa-unified@6c6acf4ddaacf65bed00eb0e100dc24bc399618f.
Unlike the original, this keeps the numInts >= 2 check so handles without
the extra ints are not read out of bounds.
---
diff --git a/src/util/u_gralloc/u_gralloc_fallback.c b/src/util/u_gralloc/u_gralloc_fallback.c
index 44fb32d..4d85683 100644
--- a/src/util/u_gralloc/u_gralloc_fallback.c
+++ b/src/util/u_gralloc/u_gralloc_fallback.c
@@ -148,8 +148,13 @@ fallback_gralloc_get_buffer_info(struct u_gralloc *gralloc,
    out->strides[0] = stride;
 
 #ifdef HAS_FREEDRENO
-   uint32_t gmsm = ('g' << 24) | ('m' << 16) | ('s' << 8) | 'm';
-   if (hnd->handle->numInts >= 2 && hnd->handle->data[hnd->handle->numFds] == gmsm) {
+   /* HACK: newer Qualcomm gralloc versions no longer store the 'gmsm' magic
+    * in the handle, so checking for it skipped UBWC detection and left
+    * UBWC buffers marked as linear (heavily distorted output). Read the
+    * UBWC flag whenever the handle has the ints for it.
+    * TODO: find another way to detect a Qualcomm vendor allocated buffer.
+    */
+   if (hnd->handle->numInts >= 2) {
       /* This UBWC flag was introduced in a5xx. */
       bool ubwc = hnd->handle->data[hnd->handle->numFds + 1] & 0x08000000;
       out->modifier = ubwc ? DRM_FORMAT_MOD_QCOM_COMPRESSED : DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR;
